# Clean URLs (required)

Keep on-disk `*.html` files for GitHub Pages. **Never expose `.html` in user-facing links.**

## Two environments

| Environment | Example |
|---|---|
| Production | `https://hurumachildrenstrustcanada.org/` |
| GitHub Pages preview | `https://collingwood-web-design.github.io/huruma-childrens-trust-canada-pages/` |

## Navigation / in-page links — path-relative (not root-relative)

| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| `href="/"` | `href="./"` |
| `href="index.html"` | `href="./"` |
| `href="../index.html"` | `href="../"` |
| `href="donate.html"` | `href="donate-now/"` (EN) or `href="donate"` (FR) |
| `href="donation-costs.html"` | `href="donation-costs"` |
| `href="mamas-health.html"` | `href="mamas-health/"` (EN) or `href="mamas-health"` (FR) |

Same-page hashes stay `#section`. Do **not** reintroduce `.html` to fix preview issues.

## SEO metadata — always production absolute clean URLs

Canonical, Open Graph, Twitter, JSON-LD, sitemap, and `llms.txt` must use:

`https://hurumachildrenstrustcanada.org/donate-now/`

Never the GitHub Pages preview host, and never `.html`.

## Assets

Leave `.css`, `.js`, images, fonts, and `.pdf` extensions alone.

## New pages

1. Prefer `pagename/index.html` (EN) or keep `pagename.html` on disk for FR flat pages.
2. Link path-relative without `.html`.
3. Keep the head script that strips a trailing `.html` from the current path.

Helpers: `python scripts/huruma-clean-urls.py`, `python scripts/apply-clean-urls.py`, `python scripts/audit-clean-urls.py`.
